.TH smi-diskless-chroot "1" "August 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Diskless Command"
.SH NAME
smi-diskless-chroot \- Run a command in the chroot of a diskless installation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-diskless-chroot
.I DISKLESS_NAME
.RI [ COMMAND
.RI [ ARGUMENTS... ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-diskless-chroot
runs
.I COMMAND
inside the chroot of the installation
.IR DISKLESS_NAME ,
or an interactive shell when no command is given.
.PP
The kernel file systems
.RB ( /proc ,
.BR /sys ,
.BR /dev ,
.B /dev/pts
and
.BR /run )
are mounted before the command and unmounted after it, and the name resolution
of the server is copied into the chroot, so package management, service
configuration and user management work exactly as on an installed machine.
.PP
This is the command behind
.BR smi-diskless-useradd (1),
.BR smi-diskless-passwd (1)
and the initramfs generation of
.BR smi-make-diskless (1).
.PP
The exit status is the exit status of
.IR COMMAND .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Enter the installation:
.RS
.B smi-diskless-chroot ws-01
.RE
.PP
Enable a service of the client:
.RS
.B smi-diskless-chroot ws-01 systemctl enable sshd
.RE
.PP
Regenerate the initramfs after a kernel update:
.RS
.nf
smi-diskless-chroot ws-01 dracut --force --no-hostonly --add "nfs network" \\
    /boot/initramfs-KERNEL_VERSION-diskless.img KERNEL_VERSION
.fi
.RE
.SH AUTHOR
.PP
Command written by Imre Tabur.
